  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1242 PM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nDry and very warm conditions roll carry into Friday as a broad \n~599 dam H5 sets up over AR into northeast TX. Not until Friday \nnight do we see this high faltering which allows monsoonal \nmoisture to creep into our westernmost counties complete with some\nrain chances. The arrival of a improved SW flow aloft on Saturday\nin the base of a broad trough cresting the Rockies spells \nimproved rain chances, especially on the Caprock, where the axis \nof monsoonal moisture overlaps with a SW-NE surface trough. This \npattern supports a regional precip event with heavy rain at times\ngiven PWAT anomalies reaching +0.5 to +0.8\" and a window for \ntraining convection. The pattern remains unsettled and turns \ncooler for Sunday following a bona fide cold front with reasonably \nmoist E-NE winds in the lowest levels. With southwest flow\nlingering aloft through early next week, additional chances for \nprecip remain intact despite mixed ensemble signals.",
